    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who commands the highest daily efficiency score at 70.30. Despite facing a difficult matchup against Abbott, his elite speed profile\u2014essential for our strategy in the scarce stolen base category\u2014is bolstered by a favorable park factor and a leadoff spot that maximizes his opportunities on the basepaths. **Casey Schmitt** also presents as a premier start with a 63.20 rating; he benefits from a significant platoon advantage against the right-handed Lorenzen, providing a high-ceiling option that comfortably clears our threshold for inclusion. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** (61.80) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (61.78) provide the core power density, with **Kazuma Okamoto** particularly poised for success against a generous 5.58 xERA from M\u00e1rquez, effectively offsetting the neutral platoon dynamics at play.\n\nThe decision to bench **Carson Benge** was the most difficult call of the morning. With a 40.59 score, he narrowly missed our active lineup; while his projection remained above the absolute floor, the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Junior Caminero** and the tactical platoon advantage afforded to **Casey Schmitt**. We are maintaining a cautious stance regarding **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**, both of whom face the formidable Skubal. While their power and plate discipline earn them spots, their scores are suppressed by Skubal\u2019s elite 2.69 xERA. Furthermore, the catchers **Gary Sanchez** and **Dillon Dingler** have been benched today, both falling below our 40.0 efficiency floor; **Dillon Dingler** specifically struggled to justify a start given his matchup against Wheeler and the negative impact of facing an elite catcher's arm, which threatens our stolen base efficiency.",
